    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Tyler Freeman** (72.25) emerges as our highest-upside play, buoyed significantly by a +14% park factor and a favorable matchup against Ray. While **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) and **Luis Arraez** (68.94) trail closely, their efficiency is driven by dynamic platoon advantages against weak arms in Kochanowicz and Gordon. We are leaning heavily into the Gordon matchup, stacking **Jung Hoo Lee** (67.73), **Matt Chapman** (67.04), and **Drew Gilbert** (54.07) against him. Despite **Drew Gilbert** hitting in the #9 hole, the confluence of a high-ceiling park and a \"Slow SP\" delivery profile\u2014which inherently boosts our stolen base probability\u2014keeps him firmly in the mix, provided he maintains his projected speed impact.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Taylor Ward** (49.36) and **Bryson Stott** (48.98). **Taylor Ward** actually benefited from a +16% park boost, but a tough draw against Miles (2.95 xERA) suppressed his upside compared to the starters. We ultimately prioritized the cumulative efficiency of **Daulton Varsho** (55.65) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (55.99) to keep our daily game-cap management in check. We remain cautious of **Daulton Varsho**; his matchup against the elite Bradish serves as a situational warning, as his efficiency is dragged down by a -19% SP skill penalty. Meanwhile, the absence of **Cal Raleigh** remains a major blow to our power metrics, leaving us to rely on our active core to generate the stolen base volume necessary to keep pace in this tight 5x5 race.",
